      "rule": "R11",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "No regression covers dropping the last non-generated column, so `CREATE TABLE t(a,b AS(5)); ALTER TABLE t DROP COLUMN a` succeeds in the model although SQLite rejects it. Fix: add native coverage and return SQLite’s dependent-table error."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261027T085243Z-6b333ba4#2",
      "line": 63,
      "path": "packages/belay-sqlite-model/Belay/Sqlite/Model/Resolution/DropColumnDependents.lean",
      "rule": "R11",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "No regression distinguishes removed CHECK constraints from surviving ones, so dropping `a` from `t(a CHECK(a>0), b, CHECK(A>0))` reports `a` instead of SQLite’s `A`. Fix: search `checksAfterDrop index` instead of `allChecks` and add an exact-message regression."
    },
